{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011CgS3JuCRjPCacQY6VmYM5","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01FD7qEaH2VrQX1xjAMfK1mw","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd /tmp/h-i9z4mz; python3 - <<'E'\nimport re\ns=open('server.py').read()\ns=s.replace('''DEFAULT_TOKEN_TTL = 3600   # seconds; used when the provider does not say how long a token lives\n''','')\ns=s.replace('''    expires_in = int(tok.get(\"expires_in\") or DEFAULT_TOKEN_TTL)\n    refresh = tok.get(\"refresh_token\")\n    if not refresh:\n        log(f\"{user_id}: no refresh_token in response, scheduling expiry in {expires_in}s\")\n''','''    # Intervals.icu tokens are long-lived: no expires_in / refresh_token means \"does not expire\".\n    expires_in = int(tok[\"expires_in\"]) if tok.get(\"expires_in\") else None\n    refresh = tok.get(\"refresh_token\")\n''')\ns=s.replace('\"expires_at\": time.time() + expires_in,','\"expires_at\": time.time() + expires_in if expires_in else None,')\ns=s.replace('(expires in {expires_in}s)\")','(expires in {expires_in}s)\" if expires_in else f\"{user_id}: connected as athlete {athlete.get(\\'id\\')} (no expiry)\")')\ns=s.replace('if c[\"status\"] != \"connected\" or c[\"expires_at\"] - now > 300:','if c[\"status\"] != \"connected\" or c[\"expires_at\"] is None or c[\"expires_at\"] - now > 300:')\ns=s.replace('expires_at=now + int(tok[\"expires_in\"]))','expires_at=now + int(tok[\"expires_in\"]) if tok.get(\"expires_in\") else None)')\ns=s.replace('''        self.redirect(AUTHORIZE_URL + \"?\" + urllib.parse.urlencode(params, safe=\":,\"))''','''        # The SPA calls this with fetch (Authorization header) and navigates to the returned URL.\n        self.send_json(200, {\"url\": AUTHORIZE_URL + \"?\" + urllib.parse.urlencode(params, safe=\":,\")})''')\nopen('server.py','w').write(s)\na=open('static/app.js').read()\na=a.replace('<a class=\"btn\" href=\"/api/intervals/auth/init\">Connect Intervals.icu</a>','<button class=\"btn\" id=\"connect\">Connect Intervals.icu</button>')\na=a.replace('''    const d = document.getElementById(\"disconnect\");''','''    const c = document.getElementById(\"connect\");\n    if (c) c.onclick = async () => {\n      try { window.location.href = (await api(\"/api/intervals/auth/init\")).url; }\n      catch (e) { root.innerHTML = `<p class=\"card\">Error: ${esc(e.message)}</p>`; }\n    };\n    const d = document.getElementById(\"disconnect\");''')\nopen('static/app.js','w').write(a)\nc=open('config.py').read()\nc=c.replace('\"ACTIVITY:READ,ACTIVITY:WRITE,WELLNESS:READ,CALENDAR:READ,CALENDAR:WRITE\"','\"ACTIVITY:WRITE,WELLNESS:READ,CALENDAR:WRITE\"')\nopen('config.py','w').write(c)\nE\ncat > ANSWER.md <<'E'\n# Why Intervals.icu connect fails\n\n1. **Connect button gets 401 for everyone.** It was a plain `<a href=\"/api/intervals/auth/init\">`. A browser navigation can't send the `Authorization: Bearer` header (the token lives in localStorage and is only added by the SPA's `fetch` wrapper), so the server answered `{\"error\":\"unauthorized\"}`. Fix: the button now calls `auth/init` via `api()`, the endpoint returns `{\"url\": ...}`, and the SPA navigates to it.\n\n2. **Authorize URL rejected with 400 `invalid_request` since the calendar sync (2026-10-02).** The only thing that changed is `SCOPES`, which gained `CALENDAR:READ,CALENDAR:WRITE` on top of redundant `ACTIVITY:READ` + `ACTIVITY:WRITE`. The scope string is the likely culprit (the format that worked for Rivera was `ACTIVITY:WRITE,WELLNESS:READ`, where a WRITE scope stands alone). I trimmed it to `ACTIVITY:WRITE,WELLNESS:READ,CALENDAR:WRITE`. **Unverified:** I can't call Intervals.icu from here, and its error body doesn't name the bad parameter. If it still 400s, test scope sets against the authorize URL one at a time.\n\n3. **\"Reconnect after an hour\".** Intervals.icu's token response has no `expires_in` and no `refresh_token` (see Rivera's logged response); its tokens are long-lived. `store_connection` invented a 3600s TTL (`DEFAULT_TOKEN_TTL`), and the refresher then marked the connection expired because there was no refresh token. Fix: no `expires_in` means no expiry (`expires_at=None`), and the refresher skips such connections. The refresh path also no longer crashes on a response lacking `expires_in`.\n\nNot tested end to end against the real Intervals.icu.\nE\npython3 -c \"import ast;ast.parse(open('server.py').read())\"; git diff --stat"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":6141,"cache_read_input_tokens":22359,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":6141},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"c42262a3-62eb-42cd-b4a6-51afc5742c26","uuid":"10007fb4-ebab-4c3b-84a9-56fd243c7d78","timestamp":"2026-10-27T03:35:19.574Z","request_id":"req_011CgS3JtxnUTp6iLdXurdJD","wire_tool_inputs":{"toolu_01FD7qEaH2VrQX1xjAMfK1mw":{"command":"cd /tmp/h-i9z4mz; python3 - <<'E'\nimport re\ns=open('server.py').read()\ns=s.replace('''DEFAULT_TOKEN_TTL = 3600   # seconds; used when the provider does not say how long a token lives\n''','')\ns=s.replace('''    expires_in = int(tok.get(\"expires_in\") or DEFAULT_TOKEN_TTL)\n    refresh = tok.get(\"refresh_token\")\n    if not refresh:\n        log(f\"{user_id}: no refresh_token in response, scheduling expiry in {expires_in}s\")\n''','''    # Intervals.icu tokens are long-lived: no expires_in / refresh_token means \"does not expire\".\n    expires_in = int(tok[\"expires_in\"]) if tok.get(\"expires_in\") else None\n    refresh = tok.get(\"refresh_token\")\n''')\ns=s.replace('\"expires_at\": time.time() + expires_in,','\"expires_at\": time.time() + expires_in if expires_in else None,')\ns=s.rep